            <ArticleTitle>Lipoma of the Tendon Sheath in the Fourth Extensor Compartment of the Hand.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>561-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lipoma of an extensor tendon compartment is an exceedingly rare tumor of the hand. Although benign, it can often cause localized pain and finger stiffness, necessitating surgical excision. We report a case of a lipoma of the tendon sheath in the fourth dorsal compartment of the hand that was successfully treated with surgical excision.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
